From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 07:53:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: apple: isp: restart a T8132 stream after sleep
 from a work item

On T8132 the ISP firmware boots afresh for every stream and is powered
down when the stream stops, so a stream that ran across a system sleep
is restarted on resume with a cold firmware boot of a second or more.
That boot currently runs inside the resume callback and holds up the
rest of the system's resume.

Resident firmware already restarts from a freezable work item once tasks
thaw. Use the same work item for a stream that was sleeping on hardware
with the per-stream power-down. Nothing changes when no stream ran
across the sleep, or on other machines.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
(cherry picked from commit d25181d87c8e47016521ada915905db64b19e5dd)
---
 drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-drv.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-drv.c b/drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-drv.c
index 3b1a12a884..d95898fe0a 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-drv.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-drv.c
@@ -1605,6 +1605,15 @@ static __maybe_unused int apple_isp_resume(struct device *dev)
 		queue_work(system_freezable_wq, &isp->resume_work);
 		return 0;
 	}
+	/*
+	 * Where the firmware boots afresh for every stream (T8132), restarting
+	 * a stream that ran across the sleep is a cold boot of a second or
+	 * more; do it from the same work item, not in the resume path.
+	 */
+	if (isp->hw->macos_stop && test_bit(ISP_STATE_SLEEPING, &isp->state)) {
+		queue_work(system_freezable_wq, &isp->resume_work);
+		return 0;
+	}
 	apple_isp_video_resume(isp);
 
 	return 0;
